          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.286,
            0.12,
            0.884,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": "same one roti, each child gets a smaller share. So, $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ roti is more than ${ \\textstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } } \\; r o t i .$ 12 > 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.199,
            0.72,
            0.225
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "7.1 Fractional Units and Equal Shares"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.242,
            0.66,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "Beni: Which fraction is greater — $\\frac{1}{5}$ or $\\frac { 1 } { 9 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.268,
            0.884,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": "Arvin: 9 is bigger than 5. So I would guess that $\\frac { 1 } { 9 }$ is greater than $\\frac { 1 } { 5 } . \\mathrm { A m }$ I right?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.314,
            0.884,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "Beni: No! That is a common mistake. Think of these fractions as shares."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.356,
            0.884,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "Arvin: If one roti is shared among 5 children, each one gets a share of $\\frac{1}{5}$ roti. If one roti is shared among 9 children, each one gets a share of $\\frac{1}{9}$ roti?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.424,
            0.821,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "Beni: Exactly! Now think again - which share is higher?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.448,
            0.837,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "Arvin: If I share with more people, I will get less. So, $\\textstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 9 } } < { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.472,
            0.406,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "Beni: You got it!"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.511,
            0.649,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Oh,~s0~\\frac{1}{100}~is~bigger~than~\\frac{1}{200}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.558,
            0.884,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": "When one unit is divided into several equal parts, each part is called a **fractional unit**. These are all fractional units:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.609,
            0.561,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{5}, \\frac{1}{6}, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{10}, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{50}, \\ldots, \\frac{1}{100}, \\text { etc. }",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.649,
            0.83,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": "We also sometimes refer to fractional units as ‘**unit fractions**."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.682,
            0.353,
            0.704
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.712,
            0.524,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "Fill in the blanks with fractions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.735,
            0.883,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "1. Three guavas together weigh 1 kg. If they are roughly of the same size, each guava will roughly weigh \\_\\_\\_\\_ kg."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.782,
            0.809,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "2. A wholesale merchant packed 1 kg of rice in four packets of equal weight. The weight of each packet is \\_\\_\\_ kg."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.825,
            0.809,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": "3. Four friends ordered 3 glasses of sugarcane juice and shared it equally among themselves. Each one drank glass of sugarcane juice."
        },
        {
